+# Contract: `POST /v1/executions/{id}/signal` — recognized-retry reply
+
+**Feature**: [../spec.md](../spec.md) | **Data model**: [../data-model.md](../data-model.md) | **Date**: 2026-10-27
+
+This contract documents the public management-API surface the feature touches: one endpoint, its full set of reply variants, and — marked **CHANGED** — the single additive behavior introduced by this feature. All other variants are **UNCHANGED** and remain byte-for-byte the established shapes; consumers must keep working without edits (SC-003).
+
+## Endpoint
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Method / path | `POST /v1/executions/{id}/signal` |
+| Service | `graphhelm serve` (local management API, loopback by construction) |
+| Auth | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (the token the server wrote beside the events directory); everything but `/health` refuses without it (401). |
+| Route command identity | `"execution.signal"` (reported as `command` in every reply for this route) |
+
+### Request
+
+Headers:
+
+| Header | Required | Value |
+|---|---|---|
+| `Idempotency-Key` | yes | ≤ 64 chars; caller-chosen; reusing it with an identical body + actor is what makes a retry *recognised* |
+| `X-GraphHelm-Actor` | yes | actor id the committed event is attributed to |
+| `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type` | yes | `owner` or `agent` (closed set) |
+| `If-Match` | no | expected stream head (u64); checked only on fresh commands, ignored for recognised retries |
+
+Body:
+
+```json
+{
+  "signal": {
+    "id": "<caller-chosen signal identifier (OpaqueId)>",
+    "source": { "type": "node", "id": "<node id in this execution>" },
+    "type": "<signal kind string>",
+    "severity": "<severity>",
+    "description": "<free text (externalized evidence)>",
+    "evidence": ["<evidence reference>"],
+    "emittedAt": "<ISO-8601 timestamp>"
+  },
+  "evidenceOut": "<path on the Runtime host (required unless the server runs with a sealed keyring)>"
+}
+```
+
+Missing/invalid headers → 400 envelope before any store access; body must be valid JSON carrying `signal`.
+
+### Reply envelope (all variants)
+
+```json
+{ "ok": true|false, "command": "execution.signal", "data": { ... }, "diagnostics": [ { "code": "...", "message": "...", "path": "<JSON pointer>", "source": "..." } ] }
+```
+
+The JSON envelope is the machine-readable contract for non-terminal consumers; this feature only ever adds a field inside `data`, never changes the envelope itself.
+
+## Reply variants
+
+### V1 — Fresh success (`200`, first time for this key) — UNCHANGED
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": true,
+  "command": "execution.signal",
+  "data": {
+    "executionId": "exec-...",
+    "signalId": "sig-42",
+    "kind": "no_progress",
+    "mayProposeMutation": true,
+    "decision": "accept",
+    "headSequence": 43
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Carries `signalId`, never an `idempotency` marker (FR-005). `rejectionReason` appears only when `decision` is `"rejected"`.
+
+### V2 — Recognised-retry success (`200`, same key + body + actor already committed) — **CHANGED (additive only)**
+
+Pre-change shape: current execution status projection + `idempotency` proof, **no** `signalId`.
+Post-change shape: the same, plus one field:
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": true,
+  "command": "execution.signal",
+  "data": {
+    "...current execution status projection (unchanged fields)...": "...",
+    "headSequence": 57,
+    "idempotency": {
+      "recognizedRetry": true,
+      "originalDecisionSequence": 42
+    },
+    "signalId": "sig-42"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Contract deltas, precisely:
+
+| Aspect | Before | After |
+|---|---|---|
+| `data.signalId` | absent | **present**: the original durable identifier, verbatim from the committed `signal_recorded` record's payload — identical byte-for-byte to V1's `data.signalId` for the same submission, independent of how far the stream has advanced since |
+| everything else in `data` (status projection, `headSequence`, `idempotency` block and its two fields) | as established | byte-for-byte unchanged (FR-006) |
+| HTTP status, `ok`, `command`, diagnostics on success | as established | unchanged |
+| repeatable behaviour | — | every retry of the same key returns the same `data.signalId` (multiple retries, stream advanced or not) |
+
+Semantics:
+- Retrieval is read-only over the append-only store; a recognised retry appends nothing.
+- A stale `If-Match` on a recognised retry is still ignored (outcome already fixed).
+- If recovery of the identifier fails on a recognised signal retry (defensive, unreachable while classification holds its guarantees), the reply is the structured failure below (V5) rather than a silently incomplete V2 (research R4).
+
+### V3 — Refusal: partial previous attempt (`409`) — UNCHANGED
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": false,
+  "command": "execution.signal",
+  "data": { "currentHead": 57 },
+  "diagnostics": [ { "code": "GHE003_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT", "message": "a previous attempt at this command applied only part of it; ...", "path": "/idempotencyKey", "source": "..." } ]
+}
+```
+
+No `idempotency` block, no `signalId`, nothing appended.
+
+### V4 — Refusal: divergent reuse (mismatched actor, body, execution/scope, or decision kind) (`409`) — UNCHANGED
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": false,
+  "command": "execution.signal",
+  "data": { "currentHead": 57 },
+  "diagnostics": [ { "code": "GHE003_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT", "message": "the Idempotency-Key \"...\" is already committed to a different authenticated mutation identity; ...", "path": "/idempotencyKey", "source": "..." } ]
+}
+```
+
+Non-disclosure rule (FR-003/FR-004 + spec edge case): the reply names only the caller's own bare header value and head position — it must contain neither the original actor, nor the original `signalId`, nor the mismatched event kind.
+
+### V5 — Defensive internal failure (`500`) — UNCHANGED code/path; condition extended
+
+The existing arm used when a recognised retry's status cannot carry its proof gains one reachable-in-principle trigger: a recognised signal retry from which the signal identifier could not be recovered.
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": false,
+  "command": "execution.signal",
+  "diagnostics": [ { "code": "GHCLI023_IDEMPOTENCY_REPLY_INVALID", "message": "...", "path": "/data", "source": "..." } ]
+}
+```
+
+No new diagnostic code is introduced by this feature.
+
+### V6 — Recognised-retry replies of other mutation kinds (`200`) — UNCHANGED
+
+`start`, `approve`, `amend_budget`, `pause`, `resume`, `cancel`, `sweep`, `wake_lease`, `claim`, `clear`: today's exact shape (status projection + `idempotency` proof). `data.signalId` does not appear in any of them (FR-007). No contract text beyond this sentence changes for those routes.
+
+## Consumer impact summary
+
+| Consumer situation | Impact |
+|---|---|
+| Client that saw V1, lost the ack, retried, and now reads `data.signalId` off *either* reply | Works with one client rule: "read the signal identifier from `data.signalId`" (spec edge case: naming consistency) |
+| Any existing consumer of any other variant | Zero edits: byte-for-byte stable (SC-003) |
+| New consumer relying on `data.signalId` presence in V2 | New capability introduced by this feature |
