+# Phase 1 Data Model: Recognized Signal Retry Returns Original Signal Id
+
+**Feature**: [spec.md](spec.md) | **Plan**: [plan.md](plan.md) | **Date**: 2026-10-27
+
+No entity, table, file layout, or wire schema is added by this feature. The model below documents the **existing** entities the change reads and writes, the one additive field, and the classification state machine that decides which reply variant a request receives. Source of truth for field spellings: `core/protocols/src/event.rs`, `apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs`, `apps/cli/src/commands/execution/signal.rs`.
+
+## Entities
+
+### E1 — Signal submission request (transient, per HTTP request)
+
+The caller's intent to record a signal at `POST /v1/executions/{id}/signal`.
+
+| Field | Type | Validation / notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `Idempotency-Key` (header) | string, ≤ 64 chars | Required. The *bare* header. A derived event key is built as `{header}-record-{digest16}` where `digest16` is 16 hex chars over execution id + body (divergence detector, not a security boundary). |
+| `X-GraphHelm-Actor` (header) | actor id string | Required. Durable attribution of the committed event. |
+| `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type` (header) | `owner` \| `agent` | Required. Closed set; anything else is 400 before store access. |
+| `If-Match` (header, optional) | u64 | Advisory fast-fail against the stream head, checked only for genuinely fresh commands; ignored for recognised retries whose outcome is already fixed. |
+| body `signal` | object | Required. Envelope: `{ id, source: { type: "node", id }, type, severity, description, evidence[], emittedAt }` — validated by `admit_signal`; its SHA-256 binds the record. |
+| body `evidenceOut` | path string \| absent | Required when the server has no sealed keyring (otherwise the route refuses before appending). |
+| authenticated bearer token | — | Standard serve auth; everything but `/health` refuses without it. |
+
+**Relationships**: identifies at most one committed decision record (E2) via the derived key + full-identity match.
+
+### E2 — Committed signal decision record (durable, append-only)
+
+The `signal_recorded` event appended exactly once by the original successful submission. It is the single source of truth for "what did the original attempt record" and the **recovery source for this feature**.
+
+Wire shape (as rendered in the events feed):
+
+```json
+{
+  "sequence": 42,
+  "idempotencyKey": "<bare-header>-record-<digest16>",
+  "actor": { "type": "agent", "id": "<actor-id>" },
+  "kind": {
+    "type": "signal_recorded",
+    "data": {
+      "executionId": "<execution-id>",
+      "signalId": "<caller-chosen signal identifier>",
+      "sourceKind": "node",
+      "sourceId": "<node-id>",
+      "kind": "<signal type string, e.g. no_progress>",
+      "severity": "high",
+      "envelopeSha256": "sha256:<64 hex>"
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+| Field | Notes |
+|---|---|
+| `sequence` | Monotonic u64 within the execution stream. Becomes `originalDecisionSequence` in retry proofs. |
+| `idempotencyKey` | Derived key (E1). Exact equality is the first half of retry authentication. |
+| `actor` | Must equal the retrying request's authenticated actor, else refusal (FR-003). |
+| `kind.type` | Must be `signal_recorded` for a signal retry, else wrong-kind refusal (FR-004). |
+| **`kind.data.signalId`** | **The value this feature surfaces.** Written once at append time from the admitted envelope's `id`; opaque (`OpaqueId`: non-empty, ≤ 128 bytes, closed character set). Never recomputed on read (FR-002). |
+| `kind.data.envelopeSha256` | Binds the record to the exact committed envelope bytes; the retry's envelope must hash identically. |
+
+**Invariants**:
+- Append-only: never rewritten by projections, Dreams, or retries.
+- Retry authentication (`ExpectedDecision::matches`) requires ALL of: exact derived-key equality, equal actor, equal scope/stream, equal execution id, and the full kind-specific binding above (including `signal.id == signalId` and envelope digest equality).
+- No new storage: the feature reads E2, writes nothing.
+
+### E3 — Fresh signal reply (200, first-time key)
+
+Shape produced by `execution::signal::execute`, then augmented by the mutation runner:
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": true,
+  "command": "execution.signal",
+  "data": {
+    "executionId": "<execution-id>",
+    "signalId": "<same value as E2.kind.data.signalId>",
+    "kind": "<signal type>",
+    "mayProposeMutation": true,
+    "decision": "accept",
+    "headSequence": 43
+  }
+}
+```
+
+(`rejectionReason` appears only for `decision == "rejected"`.) **Unchanged by this feature** (FR-005). It is also the *naming/location precedent*: `data.signalId` is where a client reads "the signal I sent" — the retry reply must expose the same value at the same pointer.
+
+### E4 — Recognized-retry reply (200, recognised repeat) — THE CHANGED ENTITY
+
+Constructed from the current `execution.status` projection plus the retry proof; the feature adds one field:
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": true,
+  "command": "execution.signal",
+  "data": {
+    "...current execution status projection...": "...(execution aggregate, incl. headSequence)...",
+    "headSequence": 57,
+    "idempotency": {
+      "recognizedRetry": true,
+      "originalDecisionSequence": 42
+    },
+    "signalId": "<E2.kind.data.signalId, verbatim>"   // <-- NEW in this feature, additive
+  }
+}
+```
+
+**Rules**:
+- `signalId` appears **iff** the request's command is `execution.signal` **and** recovery from E2 succeeded (research R3). Value is recovered verbatim from E2, never echoed from the request (FR-002).
+- Everything else in the reply — status projection, `idempotency` block (identified by committed sequence only), `headSequence` — is unchanged (FR-006). The proof keeps naming the original decision by sequence; `signalId` rides beside it.
+- The same shape is produced by both call sites that can classify a retry: the pre-flight `Complete` arm and the post-append-race re-classification arm. Every retry of the same key returns the same value (edge case: multiple retries).
+
+### E5 — Refusal replies (409, unchanged — non-disclosure)
+
+`KeyState::Partial` and `KeyState::Divergent` both answer through their existing dedicated builders, which this feature does not touch:
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": false,
+  "command": "execution.signal",
+  "data": { "currentHead": 57 },
+  "diagnostics": [
+    {
+      "code": "GHE003_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT",
+      "message": "...",
+      "path": "/idempotencyKey",
+      "source": "..."
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+**Rules**: no `idempotency` block, no `signalId`, no original actor, no mismatched-kind name anywhere in the reply (FR-003/FR-004 + spec edge case "refusals leak nothing"). `data` carries only the caller-facing head position.
+
+### E6 — Other mutations' recognized-retry replies (200, unchanged)
+
+Every non-signal command (`start`, `approve`, `amend_budget`, `pause`, `resume`, `cancel`, `sweep`, `wake_lease`, `claim`, `clear`) keeps today's byte-for-byte established shape: status projection + `idempotency` block, no `signalId` (FR-007). Structural guarantee: a non-signal command's first decision key can only ever match its own event kind, never `signal_recorded`.
+
+### E7 — Defensive failure (500, fail-closed seam)
+
+If a recognised signal retry somehow yields no recoverable identifier (unreachable by construction today): `ok: false`, diagnostic `GHCLI023_IDEMPOTENCY_REPLY_INVALID` at `/data` — the code/path the reply annotator already uses when the status cannot carry its proof (research R4).
+
+## State transitions (per request, inside `run_idempotent_mutation_inner`)
+
+```text
+                       ┌─────────────────────────────┐
+   POST /signal ──────►│ classify_existing_keys       │  single scan of the raw history
+                       │ (expected identity from      │  (already performed today)
+                       │  headers + body + executor)  │
+                       └──────────────┬───────────────┘
+        ┌──────────────┬───────────────┼────────────────┬──────────────────────┐
+        ▼              ▼               ▼                ▼                      ▼
+     Absent         Complete(seq)     Partial(stuck)  Divergent(header)     lookup error
+        │              │               │                │                      │
+        ▼              ▼               ▼                ▼                      ▼
+  fresh command   RECOGNISED RETRY   409 conflict     409 conflict          failure reply
+  path (incl.     reply (E4) —       (GHE003, names   (GHE003, names        (E5-style)
+  If-Match check;  NEW: data.signalId first missing    the caller's own
+  on success:     recovered from the key); appends     bare header);
+  append E2 +     decision event E2,  nothing          appends nothing
+  presence decl., verbatim
+                  plus unchanged
+                  status + proof
+
+  (post-append race: a GHE003 from the store itself re-classifies and
+   lands in one of the same four states — same replies as above)
+```
+
+Unchanged states/transitions are marked by reference to the entities they produce (E2–E7); the only behavioral delta in the machine is that `Complete` additionally carries E2's `signalId` for insertion into E4.
+
+## Data flow summary
+
+```text
+request (E1) ──classify──► matched event = E2 ──recover .signal_id (verbatim)──►
+                                                                     │
+status projection (current state) ──annotate──► E4 data: status + idempotency proof + signalId ◄─┘
+refusals: Partial/Divergent ──► E5 (untouched builders, non-disclosing)
+```
