+| 3 | Stable diagnostics: code + stable path; tests assert codes/paths, not prose alone | PASS | No new diagnostics; the defensive arm reuses `GHCLI023_IDEMPOTENCY_REPLY_INVALID` at `/data` (existing convention in `annotate_recognized_retry`). New assertions observe field presence/value and diagnostic codes. |
+| 4 | Deterministic enforcement; no LLM/prompt/provider/model/network on validation or retry paths | PASS | Recovery is a lookup over already-loaded history slices; no I/O beyond what exists today. |
+| 5 | Core depends on interfaces, no circular crates; Studio uses only public Runtime contracts | PASS | Edit is confined to `apps/cli` (serve layer + its integration test); no cross-crate edge changes, no new dependencies. |
+| 6 | Secrets never appear in wire payloads, logs, fixtures, crash output | PASS | The value surfaced is a caller-chosen opaque identifier already present in the fresh reply and in the public events feed; refusals leak nothing new (asserted). |
+| 7 | Every public method has working behavior in the same commit; no TODO/scaffold/empty handlers | PASS | The edit extends private functions whose behavior lands with their observer test in the same commit. |
+| 8 | Documentation in English | PASS | All artifacts of this feature (plan, research, data model, contracts, quickstart, tests' doc comments) are English. |
+| 9 | Tests: fixed clock/IDs, deterministic, no internet/Docker/browser/wall-clock dependence | PASS | Regression test reuses the existing loopback child-process harness and fixed-ID helpers in `api_http.rs`; assertions compare concrete values, not timestamps or random IDs. |
+| 10 | Smallest adequate proof; no universal ceremony; prove RED → GREEN for the observed behavior | PASS | One focused end-to-end regression scenario is the correct observer for an HTTP response-shape promise (research R6); it fails pre-change and passes post-change (SC-004). |
+| 11 | Keel proportionality: bounded direct-route change | PASS | Paths in scope: the two files above. Promise: FR-001..FR-008. Proving commands: `cargo +1.97.1 test -p graphhelm-cli --test api_http --locked <filter>` then without filter. No new module, type, public function, dependency, or test file (new *test* inside an existing file). |
+
+**Result**: no unjustified violations — gate passes for Phase 0 entry.
+
+**Re-checked after Phase 1 design** (data-model.md, contracts/, quickstart.md): the design introduces no new entity, storage, endpoint, diagnostic code, dependency, or public surface beyond the additive field already gated above; the defensive 500 arm is gated on the same condition the existing arm uses. **No new violations.**
+
