+# Quickstart / Validation Guide: Recognized Signal Retry Returns Original Signal Id
+
+**Feature**: [spec.md](spec.md) | **Plan**: [plan.md](plan.md) | **Contracts**: [contracts/signal-retry-reply.md](contracts/signal-retry-reply.md) | **Date**: 2026-10-27
+
+This is a validation/run guide: the smallest checks that observe each promise of the feature, in RED → GREEN order. It is not an implementation guide — code changes live in `apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs` and the regression test in `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs` (see plan's Project Structure). Reply-shape references are in the contract; entity definitions in [data-model.md](data-model.md).
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+Rust toolchain 1.97.1 with `rustfmt`/`clippy` (install per AGENTS.md if absent):
+
+```powershell
+rustup toolchain install 1.97.1 --profile minimal --component rustfmt clippy
+```
+
+No internet, Docker, credentials, browser session, or production infrastructure is required: the test harness drives the built binary on loopback only.
+
+## Observer inventory (promise → check → command)
+
+| Promise (spec) | Observer | Command |
+|---|---|---|
+| FR-001/FR-002/FR-006 — recognised retry returns the original `signalId` verbatim, everything else unchanged | New regression scenario, retry section | Scenario A steps 3–5 below (single-test run) |
+| FR-003 — actor-mismatch refusal: no proof, no identifier, nothing appended | Same scenario, refusal section; existing actor-binding test | Single-test run; then file-wide run |
+| FR-004 — wrong-kind evidence: no proof, no identifier, nothing appended | Same scenario, wrong-kind section; existing wrong-kind test | Single-test run; then file-wide run |
+| FR-005 — fresh submissions unchanged (identifier, no retry marker) | Existing fresh-signal tests + scenario's fresh section | File-wide run |
+| FR-007 — other mutation kinds' retry replies unchanged | Existing byte-pinned retry tests for other kinds + scenario's pause-retry section | File-wide run |
+| SC-004 — scenario fails without the change | Scenario A step 1 (RED on unmodified `serve/mod.rs`) | Single-test run before applying the fix |
+| SC-003 — zero assertion edits outside additions | Review of the diff to `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs` + green file-wide run | `git diff --check` + file-wide run |
+
+## Scenario A — The regression scenario (RED → GREEN)
+
+All commands from the repository root, Windows PowerShell, pinned toolchain.
+
+### Step 1 — RED: add the regression test against unmodified serve code
+
+Add the new integration test to `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs` (per plan/research R6, reusing this file's existing helpers — `serve`, `cli_start`, `signal_envelope`, `post_json`, `head_sequence`, `last_event_of_kind`, `append_wrong_decision_kind`). Run it against the **unmodified** `serve/mod.rs`:
+
+```powershell
+cargo +1.97.1 test -p graphhelm-cli --test api_http --locked <new-test-name>
+```
+
+**Expected**: FAIL. The failing assertion is the recognised-retry one — `data.signalId` absent from the retry reply while present in the first reply (`retry_reply["data"]["signalId"] != first_reply["data"]["signalId"]`). A different failure (e.g. a harness panic or an unrelated assertion) means the test itself is defective — fix the test before any production change and re-run this step.
+
+### Step 2 — GREEN: apply the serve-layer change, re-run
+
+Apply the classification/reply change in `apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs` (capture the committed `SignalRecorded.signal_id` in `KeyState::Complete`, forward it through `reply_with_current_status` into the recognised-retry annotation, insert `data.signalId` for the signal command, fail closed otherwise). Re-run:
+
+```powershell
+cargo +1.97.1 test -p graphhelm-cli --test api_http --locked <new-test-name>
+```
+
+**Expected**: PASS, including every sub-section:
+- recognised retry (stream advanced): `data.idempotency` exactly `{ recognizedRetry: true, originalDecisionSequence: <original seq> }`, `data.headSequence` = advanced head, **`data.signalId` == first reply's `signalId` == committed event's `kind.data.signalId`**, head unchanged after the retry;
+- a second identical retry returns the same `data.signalId`;
+- actor mismatch → 409 `GHE003_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT`, no `idempotency`, **no `data.signalId`**, reply text names neither original actor nor signal id, head unchanged;
+- wrong-kind key (via the existing helper) → 409, no proof, **no `data.signalId`**, head unchanged, mismatched kind not exposed;
+- a recognised retry of a non-signal mutation (`pause`) carries its established proof and **no** `data.signalId`.
+
+Also run the serve module's own unit tests for the reply path, which pin the defensive 500 arm:
+
+```powershell
+cargo +1.97.1 test -p graphhelm-cli --locked serve::tests::a_non_object_retry_status_is_a_serialized_structured_500_response
+```
+
+(plus any new in-process companion test for the recovery-failure arm, mirroring that test's shape).
+
+### Step 3 — SC-003: whole end-to-end API suite
+
+```powershell
+cargo +1.97.1 test -p graphhelm-cli --test api_http --locked
+```
+
+**Expected**: PASS with no edits to any pre-existing assertion (only additions inside the new test function). This file is the observable contract for all mutation endpoints' idempotency semantics — any failure here is a regression, not noise.
+
+### Step 4 — Scope hygiene
+
+```powershell
+git diff --check
+git diff --stat
+```
+
+**Expected**: whitespace clean; changed paths limited to `apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs` and `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs` (plus this feature's `specs/001-bench` artifacts). No new dependencies (confirm `Cargo.toml`/`Cargo.lock` untouched), no core-crate diff.
+
+## Scenario B — Optional live HTTP walkthrough (manual proof, loopback)
+
+Drives the same journey by hand against a real `graphhelm serve`. Uses the binary the test build already produced (`target\debug\graphhelm.exe`); all state under one throwaway directory.
+
+```powershell
+$d = "C:\Users\gabri\AppData\Local\Temp\opencode\quickstart-signal-retry"; New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force $d | Out-Null
+$exe = Join-Path (Get-Location) "target\debug\graphhelm.exe"
+
+# 1) start an execution against the two-node fixture graph (same invocation the test harness uses)
+@{ nodeOutcomes = @{ implementation = "success"; deploy = "success" } } |
+  ConvertTo-Json -Depth 4 | Set-Content -Encoding ascii "$d\fixtures.json"
+& $exe execution start --file examples\graphs\manual-override-deploy.yaml --events "$d\events" `
+    --fixtures "$d\fixtures.json" --mode supervised --execution exec-qstart
+
+# 2) run the server (token lands at $d\events.token; startup envelope prints the bound address)
+& $exe serve --events "$d\events" --bind 127.0.0.1:8642
+# -> read base URL from the "serve.started" stdout line; grab the token:
+$token = Get-Content "$d\events.token" -Raw
+$base  = "http://127.0.0.1:8642"   # or the address the startup envelope actually printed
+
+# 3) first submission (evidenceOut is required without a sealed keyring)
+$body = @{
+  signal = @{
+    id = "sig-qstart-1"; source = @{ type = "node"; id = "implementation" }
+    type = "no_progress"; severity = "high"
+    description = "deploy stage needs manual review"; evidence = @("exec-1")
+    emittedAt = "2026-08-13T00:00:00Z"
+  }
+  evidenceOut = "$d\evidence.json"
+} | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 8
+curl.exe -s -X POST "$base/v1/executions/exec-qstart/signal" `
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer $token" -H "Content-Type: application/json" `
+  -H "Idempotency-Key: qstart-sig-1" -H "X-GraphHelm-Actor: agent-qstart" -H "X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type: agent" `
+  --data "$body"
+# -> V1: 200, data.signalId == "sig-qstart-1", no data.idempotency
+
+# 4) advance the stream, then retry byte-identically (same key/body/actor)
+#    ...send one further unrelated mutation (any endpoint that appends, e.g. a second signal
+#    under a different Idempotency-Key)...
+# then POST exactly the same request as step 3 again.
+# -> V2: 200, data.idempotency = { recognizedRetry: true, originalDecisionSequence: <seq> },
+#    data.headSequence advanced, AND data.signalId == "sig-qstart-1"   <-- the feature
+```
+
+**Expected outcomes** mirror contract variants V1/V2/V4: step 3 gives V1; the retry gives V2 with `data.signalId`; resending with `-H "X-GraphHelm-Actor: agent-other"` gives V4 (409, no proof, no `signalId`, no original actor named in the body). Kill the server (Ctrl-C) and delete `$d` afterwards.
+
+## Reporting
+
+Per AGENTS.md proof rules, report for this feature:
+- **passed**: Scenario A steps 1–4 (name each command and result);
+- **unobserved**: nothing expected — every FR has a named observer; if the reviewer's environment cannot build `graphhelm-cli`, say so explicitly rather than substituting a weaker check.
+
+The package-scoped commands above are the smallest checks that observe this change; a workspace-wide gate remains available for the review/merge phase but is not required to observe this feature.
