+## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Client recovers its signal identity after a lost acknowledgement (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP
+
+**Goal**: On a recognised idempotent retry of `POST /v1/executions/{id}/signal` (same key, same body, same actor), the 200 reply additionally carries the original durable `signalId` in `data.signalId`, verbatim from the originally committed `signal_recorded` record — so a retrier correlates its own submission with the durable record (FR-001, FR-002, FR-006). Refusals (mismatched actor / wrong-kind) get no proof and no identifier (FR-003, FR-004).
+
+**Independent Test**: Drive the signal endpoint end-to-end over the public API (loopback): submit a signal, advance the stream with unrelated activity, re-send the byte-identical request from the same actor, and verify the second response contains the retry proof **and** the same `data.signalId` the first response carried. Verifiable on its own by one test in `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs`.
