+## Dependencies & Execution Order
+
+### Phase Dependencies
+
+- **Setup & Baseline (Phase 1)**: No dependencies — start immediately.
+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Phase 1 (baseline). BLOCKS all user stories until the recovery plumbing is confirmed.
+- **User Story 1 (Phase 3)**: Depends on Phase 2 completion. Internal order is strict: T004 (author test) → T005 (confirm RED) → T006→T007→T008→T009→T010 (implementation, single file) → T011 (companion unit test) → T012 (confirm GREEN).
+- **User Story 2 (Phase 4)**: Depends on Phase 3's implementation landing (it observes the additive behavior and proves non-regression). Its three verification tasks are mutually independent.
+- **Polish (Phase 5)**: Depends on both user stories being complete.
+
+### User Story Dependencies
+
+- **User Story 1 (P1)**: Can start after Phase 2. No dependency on US2. Self-contained MVP.
+- **User Story 2 (P2)**: Can begin its verification once US1's implementation is in place. Shares `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs` with US1 (US1 adds the test function; US2 only READS existing assertions and runs tests — no conflicting edits), so run it AFTER US1 rather than concurrently to keep the file single-authored at a time.
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- Tests are written and confirmed to FAIL (RED) before implementation (JPD / quickstart Step 1).
+- Recovery captured → threaded → surfaced → fail-closed, in that order (T006→T010).
+- GREEN confirmed before moving to the next priority.
